            vstore <math id="alg4.l30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{out},\vec{o}_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{out},\vec{o}_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg4.l30.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg4.l30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Store <math id="alg4.l30.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{o}_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{o}_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg4.l31" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg4.l31.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">31:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg4.l31.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg4.l31.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To compute the vector of alignment scores, we utilize the row-wise matrix multiplication <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Srivastava et al. (2020)</a></cite>, which is highly efficient for vector-matrix multiplication. This operation requires each element of the vector <math id="S3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> to be multiplied with the corresponding row vector <math id="S3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> from the transposed key matrix <math id="S3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. To accomplish this, during each iteration of the loop in line 5 of Alg. <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ 3 Vectorization of FlashAttention ‣ Vectorized FlashAttention with Low-cost Exponential Computation in RISC-V Vector Processors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we must isolate individual elements of <math id="S3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>. For this purpose, we employ the <span id="S3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">vrgather</span> instruction, which enables indexing into <math id="S3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> and broadcasting a selected element across all elements of the vector <math id="S3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{a}</annotation></semantics></math>. The alignment score vector is then computed using a multiply-and-accumulate instruction, as shown in line 8 of Alg. <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ 3 Vectorization of FlashAttention ‣ Vectorized FlashAttention with Low-cost Exponential Computation in RISC-V Vector Processors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, completing the first phase of FlashAttention’s execution for a single query vector.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">It is worth noting that, instead of the row-wise approach, a dot-product-based method could have been used. However, such an approach would generate multiple scalar values that would need to be rearranged into a single vector. This process would require several additional shift and merge operations, resulting in a greater number of inefficient vector instructions. In contrast, the row-wise multiplication algorithm directly places each computed value in its correct position within the result vector, thus minimizing the number of vector instructions required and improving overall efficiency.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In the second part, covering lines 10–13, the maximum value is computed across all elements of the vector <math id="S3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>v</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}s</annotation></semantics></math> and the previously calculated maximum that is stored in vector <math id="S3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}{oldmax}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>v</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}{oldmax}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is achieved using the <span id="S3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">vredmax</span> instruction, which, in the RISC-V ISA, stores the resulting maximum in the first element of the vector <math id="S3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>v</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}{max}</annotation></semantics></math>. To propagate this value across the entire vector, it is broadcast to all elements of <math id="S3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>v</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}{max}</annotation></semantics></math> using the <span id="S3.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">vrgather</span> instruction, as shown in line 11 of Alg. <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ 3 Vectorization of FlashAttention ‣ Vectorized FlashAttention with Low-cost Exponential Computation in RISC-V Vector Processors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Moreover, since the RISC-V ISA lacks direct support for vector exponentiation instructions, the operations in lines 12 and 13 of Alg. <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ 3 Vectorization of FlashAttention ‣ Vectorized FlashAttention with Low-cost Exponential Computation in RISC-V Vector Processors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, which compute the terms <math id="S3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{m_{i-b}-m_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{m_{i-b}-m_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\vec{s}-m_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\vec{s}-m_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, are conceptually referred to as vexp for clarity. The implementation details of these operations will be discussed in the following subsection.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">In the third part, the sum of exponents is computed using the <span id="S3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">vredsum</span> instruction in line 14 of Alg. <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ 3 Vectorization of FlashAttention ‣ Vectorized FlashAttention with Low-cost Exponential Computation in RISC-V Vector Processors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Then, in lines 17–21, the current output vector <math id="S3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{o}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{o}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is computed and stored in the vector <math id="S3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{out}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{out}</annotation></semantics></math> by applying the row-wise multiplication algorithm between the vector of exponentiated attention scores and the corresponding block of the value matrix. By the end of this part, <math id="S3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{sum}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{sum}</annotation></semantics></math> contains the term <math id="S3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j}e^{s_{i-j}-m_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j}e^{s_{i-j}-m_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is required in line 5 of Alg. <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ 2.2 FlashAttention Algorithm ‣ 2 Baseline Attention and FlashAttention algorithm ‣ Vectorized FlashAttention with Low-cost Exponential Computation in RISC-V Vector Processors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, and <math id="S3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{out}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{out}</annotation></semantics></math> holds the term <math id="S3.p8.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{j}e^{s_{i-j}-m_{i}}V[i-j-1,\ :]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j}e^{s_{i-j}-m_{i}}V[i-j-1,\ :]</annotation></semantics></math>, as defined in line 6 of Alg. <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ 2.2 FlashAttention Algorithm ‣ 2 Baseline Attention and FlashAttention algorithm ‣ Vectorized FlashAttention with Low-cost Exponential Computation in RISC-V Vector Processors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p9.1" class="ltx_p">To complete the computation described in lines 5 and 6 of Alg. <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ 2.2 FlashAttention Algorithm ‣ 2 Baseline Attention and FlashAttention algorithm ‣ Vectorized FlashAttention with Low-cost Exponential Computation in RISC-V Vector Processors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, the previously computed sum of exponents <math id="S3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i-b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i-b}</annotation></semantics></math> and output vector <math id="S3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{i-b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{i-b}</annotation></semantics></math> must be added to the newly computed terms, after applying a correction factor <math id="S3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{m_{i-b}-m_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{m_{i-b}-m_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>. To simplify this correction, we use a conditional assignment. The correction is necessary whenever the current maximum value <math id="S3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> differs from the previous maximum <math id="S3.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i-b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i-b}</annotation></semantics></math>. The result of this comparison is stored in line 16 in a vector mask. This mask controls the subsequent masked multiplication instructions that adjust the vectors <math id="S3.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{oldsum}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{oldsum}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{oldout}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{oldout}</annotation></semantics></math> based on the current maximum value, as shown in lines 22 and 25 of Alg. <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ 3 Vectorization of FlashAttention ‣ Vectorized FlashAttention with Low-cost Exponential Computation in RISC-V Vector Processors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, respectively. The corrected vectors are subsequently added to the current sum of exponents and the output vector <math id="S3.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{o}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{o}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, as illustrated in lines 23 and 26 of Alg. <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ 3 Vectorization of FlashAttention ‣ Vectorized FlashAttention with Low-cost Exponential Computation in RISC-V Vector Processors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, in the last part, the output vector <math id="S3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{o}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{o}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is normalized by dividing it by the final sum of exponents <math id="S3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, as shown in line 29 of Alg. <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ 3 Vectorization of FlashAttention ‣ Vectorized FlashAttention with Low-cost Exponential Computation in RISC-V Vector Processors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Exponent approximation</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To complete the FlashAttention kernel we need to approximate in lines 12 and 13 of Alg. <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ 3 Vectorization of FlashAttention ‣ Vectorized FlashAttention with Low-cost Exponential Computation in RISC-V Vector Processors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> the exponentials of the two maximum differences attention scores. The resulting exponentiated scores should return in the same floatint-point format as the attention score differences. In RISC-V Vector ISA there is no direct instruction to compute exponentials in vector form. This absence means that software implementations must rely on approximation techniques to perform efficiently this computation at the vector level.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the case of vectorized FlashAttention, a generic exponential function approximator is unnecessary and a custom approximation suffices, as we only need to compute attention score differences that are zero or negative. This stems from the fact that attention scores are always offset by the maximum score. Therefore, the first step is to appropriately quantize the attention score differences. Then, using the approach proposed by Blin <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Blinn (1997)</a></cite>, we compute the exponential of the quantized differences in a single step and directly convert the result into floating-point format.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.1.1 </span>Quantization of attention score differences</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In general, converting a floating-point number to its fixed-point representation requires many integer bits to accommodate the wide range of floating-point arithmetic <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Koenig et al. (2017)</a></cite>. However, in this case, we can safely clip the attention score differences to a much smaller dynamic range, as it will only be used for the computation of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{x}</annotation></semantics></math> for negative values of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. In this range, <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{x}</annotation></semantics></math> quickly converges to 0, even for small negative <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> values, i.e., <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-15}=3.1\cdot 10^{-7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3.1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-15}=3.1\cdot 10^{-7}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this work, we employ scaling quantization of the clipped attention score differences.
Each attention score difference <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is scaled by <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> and rounded. The scaling factor is defined as:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=\frac{2^{b-1}-1}{a}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=\frac{2^{b-1}-1}{a},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of bits in the fixed-point representation, and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> is the largest absolute value to be represented.
The quantized fixed-point value is then given by:</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{f}=\operatorname{int}(s\cdot\Delta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>int</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{f}=\operatorname{int}(s\cdot\Delta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For simplicity, we set <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=32</annotation></semantics></math> and choose the maximum absolute value <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> to be 256. This corresponds to a fixed-point representation with a 9-bit integer part and a 23-bit fractional part.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.1.2 </span>Exponential of quantized attention score differences</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To simplify computation, it is preferable to work with powers of two rather than natural exponents. Since <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{x}=2^{x\log_{2}e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{x}=2^{x\log_{2}e}</annotation></semantics></math>, our goal is to compute <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{x_{f}\log_{2}e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{x_{f}\log_{2}e}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> is the quantized attention score difference computed in (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3.1.1 Quantization of attention score differences ‣ 3.1 Exponent approximation ‣ 3 Vectorization of FlashAttention ‣ Vectorized FlashAttention with Low-cost Exponential Computation in RISC-V Vector Processors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), and obtain the result directly in floating-point format without any additional conversion step.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Leaving aside for now the multiplication of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log_{2}e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log_{2}e</annotation></semantics></math>, we note that since <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> is a fixed-point number with an integer part <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and a fractional part <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can express <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{x_{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{x_{f}}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{x_{f}}=2^{I_{x}+F_{x}}=2^{I_{x}}\cdot 2^{F_{x}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{x_{f}}=2^{I_{x}+F_{x}}=2^{I_{x}}\cdot 2^{F_{x}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, being a fractional part, lies between 0 and 1 by construction, we can safely approximate <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{F_{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{F_{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+F_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+F_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting this approximation into (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.1.2 Exponential of quantized attention score differences ‣ 3.1 Exponent approximation ‣ 3 Vectorization of FlashAttention ‣ Vectorized FlashAttention with Low-cost Exponential Computation in RISC-V Vector Processors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), we obtain:</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{x_{f}}\approx 2^{I_{x}}\cdot(1+F_{x})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></msup><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{x_{f}}\approx 2^{I_{x}}\cdot(1+F_{x})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">With this approximation, we observe that the result of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{x_{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{x_{f}}</annotation></semantics></math> takes the form of a floating-point number, where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the unbiased exponent and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> to the mantissa.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To fit to the floating-point representation the exponent bias must be restored affecting only the integer part <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> and leaving the fraction part <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> unchanged. As noted by Blin <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Blinn (1997)</a></cite>, this can be achieved by adding to <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> bias <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> scaled by the fraction (mantissa) bit width <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2^{x_{f}}\approx 2^{I_{x}-B}\cdot(1+F_{x})=x_{f}+B\cdot 2^{W_{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></msup><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2^{x_{f}}\approx 2^{I_{x}-B}\cdot(1+F_{x})=x_{f}+B\cdot 2^{W_{M}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">This addition effectively incorporates the exponent bias back into <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, thereby reconstructing the correct binary representation of the floating-point value of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{x}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mn>2</mn><mi>f</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{x}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg5" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 5</span> </span> Vectorized exponentiaion of attention score differences in FlashAttention</figcaption>
<div id="alg5.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg5.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg5.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
                
                
              vmfle <math id="alg5.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{mask},\ \text{v}_{exp},\ -15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{mask},\ \text{v}_{exp},\ -15</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg5.l1.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg5.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Create mask for clipping
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg5.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg5.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
                
                
              vmul <math id="alg5.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{exp},\ s\cdot\log_{2}(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{exp},\ s\cdot\log_{2}(e)</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg5.l2.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg5.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Floating point multiplication
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg5.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg5.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
                
                
              <math id="alg5.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{exp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{exp}</annotation></semantics></math> = int(<math id="alg5.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{exp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{exp}</annotation></semantics></math>)
<span id="alg5.l3.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg5.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Integer conversion
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg5.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg5.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
                
                
              vadd <math id="alg5.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{exp},\ \text{v}_{exp},\ B\cdot 2^{W_{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{exp},\ \text{v}_{exp},\ B\cdot 2^{W_{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg5.l4.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg5.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Integer addition
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg5.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg5.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
                
                
              vadd <math id="alg5.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{exp},\ \text{v}_{zero},\ e^{-15},\text{v}_{mask}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{exp},\ \text{v}_{zero},\ e^{-15},\text{v}_{mask}</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg5.l5.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg5.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Replace the clipped values of x with <math id="alg5.l5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-15}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-15}</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This implementation of vectorized exponentiation is presented in Alg. <a href="#alg5" title="Algorithm 5 ‣ 3.1.2 Exponential of quantized attention score differences ‣ 3.1 Exponent approximation ‣ 3 Vectorization of FlashAttention ‣ Vectorized FlashAttention with Low-cost Exponential Computation in RISC-V Vector Processors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. Let <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{\text{exp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mtext>exp</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{\text{exp}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the input vector containing the values that need to be exponentiated. The computation begins by identifying elements in <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{\text{exp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mtext>exp</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{\text{exp}}</annotation></semantics></math> that are less than <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-15</annotation></semantics></math>. For these elements, a mask is generated to indicate which values require clipping.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Following the mask generation, a floating-point multiplication is performed using the precomputed constant <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\cdot\log_{2}(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\cdot\log_{2}(e)</annotation></semantics></math>, effectively computing the product <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\cdot x_{\text{exp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mtext>exp</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\cdot x_{\text{exp}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This result is then converted to an integer representation, as shown in line 2 of Alg. <a href="#alg5" title="Algorithm 5 ‣ 3.1.2 Exponential of quantized attention score differences ‣ 3.1 Exponent approximation ‣ 3 Vectorization of FlashAttention ‣ Vectorized FlashAttention with Low-cost Exponential Computation in RISC-V Vector Processors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. An integer addition is subsequently performed between the converted result and the constant <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\cdot 2^{W_{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\cdot 2^{W_{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, elements of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{\text{exp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mtext>exp</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{\text{exp}}</annotation></semantics></math> that were marked for clipping are replaced. This is achieved via a masked vector operation that conditionally assigns the value <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-15}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-15}</annotation></semantics></math> to the corresponding positions, using a zero-initialized vector <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{\text{zero}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mtext>zero</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{\text{zero}}</annotation></semantics></math> to facilitate the update. For the elements not requiring clipping, the addition will not have an effect due to masking.
The final output vector approximates the exponential function <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{x}</annotation></semantics></math> for the attention score differences in the context of FlashAttention.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The five operations described in Alg. <a href="#alg5" title="Algorithm 5 ‣ 3.1.2 Exponential of quantized attention score differences ‣ 3.1 Exponent approximation ‣ 3 Vectorization of FlashAttention ‣ Vectorized FlashAttention with Low-cost Exponential Computation in RISC-V Vector Processors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, i.e., masking operation, floating-point multiplication, integer conversion, and addition, are all supported by standard RISC-V vector instructions and allows us to compute exponential functions as needed in the context of Flashattention in a cost-efficient manner.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Tiling in Vectorized FlashAttention</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since a vector engine is equipped with a finite number of arithmetic logic units (ALUs) and can operate on only a limited amount of data concurrently, the size of the input arrays often exceeds the level of parallelism the hardware can natively support. This mismatch between data volume and computational capacity necessitates the use of additional techniques to manage and optimize performance. One such method is tiling, which partitions the data into smaller, manageable blocks that fit within the engine’s parallel processing capabilities. By processing these tiles sequentially or in batches, the system ensures that the full attention output is computed correctly and efficiently.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg6" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 6</span> </span> Vectorized FlashAttention-2 with d greater than vector length</figcaption>
<div id="alg6.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg6.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg6.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg6.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for each</span> query <math id="alg6.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{q}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg6.l1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg6.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg6.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg6.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=vl:vl:N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=vl:vl:N</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg6.l2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg6.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
            
            
             <math id="alg6.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{s}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{s}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg6.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
            
            
             <span id="alg6.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg6.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=0:d/vl-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=0:d/vl-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg6.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg6.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
            
            
               <span id="alg6.l5.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">vload <math id="alg6.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">v</mtext><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg6.l5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\vec{q}\ [h\cdot vl:\ (h+1)\cdot vl-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" lspace="0.500em" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">h</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#0000FF" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">v</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" lspace="0.278em" mathcolor="#0000FF" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">h</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">v</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{q}\ [h\cdot vl:\ (h+1)\cdot vl-1]</annotation></semantics></math></span>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg6.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
            
            
               <span id="alg6.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg6.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=0:vl-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=0:vl-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg6.l6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg6.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
            
            
                <span id="alg6.l7.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">vload <math id="alg6.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">v</mtext><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg6.l7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="K^{T}[h\cdot vl+j,\ (i-vl):\ i-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">K</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">T</mi></msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">h</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#0000FF" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">v</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">v</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{T}[h\cdot vl+j,\ (i-vl):\ i-1]</annotation></semantics></math></span>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg6.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
            
            
                vrgather <math id="alg6.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{a},\ \text{v}_{q},\ j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mi>a</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mi>q</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{a},\ \text{v}_{q},\ j</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg6.l8.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg6.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Broadcast jth element of <math id="alg6.l8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{q}</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg6.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg6.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
            
            
                vmacc <math id="alg6.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{s},\ \text{v}_{k},\ \text{v}_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mi>s</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{s},\ \text{v}_{k},\ \text{v}_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg6.l9.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg6.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Multiply-Accumulate
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg6.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg6.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
            
            
               <span id="alg6.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg6.l10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg6.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg6.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
            
            
             <span id="alg6.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg6.l11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg6.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg6.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
            
            
             vredmax <math id="alg6.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{v}_{max},\ \text{v}_{s},\ \text{v}_{oldmax}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mi>s</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mtext>v</mtext><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{v}_{max},\ \text{v}_{s},\ \text{v}_{oldmax}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg6.l12.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg6.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Obtain current maximum value
</span>
</div>
